WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:04.090 --> 00:07.180
The Pokémon Center should be around here, but...

00:07.180 --> 00:08.540
...I can't see it anywhere.

00:08.540 --> 00:10.660
I wonder if the professor is already there.

00:11.630 --> 00:12.900
No worries, no worries.

00:15.160 --> 00:15.880
It came from over there.

00:16.250 --> 00:16.860
Let's go check.

00:21.370 --> 00:27.080
Mega Tabunne VS Giga Giga Nyarth!!

00:28.080 --> 00:37.930
Data broadcast giveaways for 3 weeks in a row! Today is the third giveaway, where you can receive a "level 100 Zygarde" in your video games!

00:31.990 --> 00:33.550
Somebody!

00:35.100 --> 00:37.430
Help!

00:37.430 --> 00:38.390
Are you okay?

00:39.050 --> 00:48.940
During today's data broadcast, we'll announce a "universal serial code" with which you can receive a "level 100 Zygarde" in "Pocket Monsters X/Y/OR/AS"!
Push the d-button on your remote and participate in the broadcast!

00:40.200 --> 00:41.180
We'll help you now!

00:47.350 --> 00:49.240
Please... I can't get loose.

00:51.070 --> 00:52.520
Please hold on to my hands.

00:55.830 --> 00:56.780
Heave-ho!

00:59.670 --> 01:00.480
O-Ow...

01:02.700 --> 01:03.560
You still can't get loose, huh...

01:03.930 --> 01:05.460
She must be stuck really tight.

01:06.440 --> 01:08.790
Hey bro, can't you do anything about it?

01:10.970 --> 01:12.350
I got it.

01:12.350 --> 01:15.340
I have invented a nice machine for times like this.

01:15.340 --> 01:16.720
Never mind <i>that</i>! Hurry!

01:16.940 --> 01:18.650
I get it.

01:18.940 --> 01:19.880
Please do not move.

01:24.330 --> 01:24.750
Now!

01:24.990 --> 01:25.480
All right!

01:28.920 --> 01:29.690
Here goes!

01:37.180 --> 01:37.870
Are you all right?

01:39.980 --> 01:41.080
Thank you.

01:41.830 --> 01:43.900
But how did you end up like this?

01:44.150 --> 01:44.790
The truth is...

01:45.100 --> 01:46.350
I was looking for this.

01:47.750 --> 01:48.360
What?

01:49.510 --> 01:50.790
A Mega Stone?

01:51.180 --> 01:54.280
Yeah. I've been looking for it the whole time and have finally found it.

01:54.280 --> 01:56.090
I see, so that's why.

01:56.490 --> 01:58.890
Hey, now that you mention Mega Stones... We forgot about the professor!

01:58.890 --> 02:00.410
You're right. We have to hurry.

02:00.760 --> 02:02.850
Is there a Pokémon Center nearby?

02:04.060 --> 02:05.950
If that's what you're looking for, leave it to me.

02:06.410 --> 02:08.060
I'll guide you there as a sign of gratitude.

02:08.990 --> 02:11.180
You will? Thank you so much.

02:17.560 --> 02:18.230
An ambulance?

02:21.560 --> 02:22.280
What?!

02:26.540 --> 02:28.140
I cannot believe it was you, Joy-san!

02:28.460 --> 02:29.540
I'm so surprised!

02:31.430 --> 02:34.620
I always look like that when I'm out in the field.

02:34.620 --> 02:35.510
Come on, get in!

02:36.040 --> 02:36.840
Okay!

02:42.230 --> 02:43.340
She's late...

02:45.590 --> 02:47.150
There she is! She's back!

02:50.920 --> 02:53.390
Sorry for the wait. This is the Pokémon Center.

02:59.900 --> 03:01.310
Joy-san, you were of great help.

03:01.630 --> 03:02.820
So were you.

03:04.310 --> 03:08.250
We heard there was a stupid Joy-san who often left her Pokémon Center unattended...

03:08.700 --> 03:11.960
...and thought of getting lots of Pokémon from there...

03:12.380 --> 03:15.310
Who would've thought that the even stupider brats would come along too?

03:15.310 --> 03:17.950
If we want to get Pikachu, this is our chance!

03:17.950 --> 03:19.630
Our big, big chance!

03:24.120 --> 03:27.010
Thank goodness! The professor doesn't seem to be here yet.

03:28.490 --> 03:30.680
In that case, do you want me to heal your Pokémon?

03:31.260 --> 03:32.560
Please do!

03:33.160 --> 03:35.530
All right, then please put your monster balls in here.

03:38.540 --> 03:39.640
Is something the matter?

03:40.280 --> 03:41.030
Let me see...

03:42.150 --> 03:43.070
Uh, wait...

03:48.470 --> 03:51.960
On the other side of the door, someone seems to have put up a barricade of sorts.

03:54.870 --> 03:56.140
Open up!

03:56.440 --> 03:58.210
Tabunne, this was you, right?

03:58.780 --> 03:59.400
"Tabunne"?

03:59.640 --> 04:00.960
Is there a Tabunne in there?

04:01.910 --> 04:07.430
I heard that in some other regions, Tabunne work as Joy-san's assistants.

04:08.670 --> 04:10.230
Open up, Tabunne!

04:15.910 --> 04:17.180
Geez!

04:17.180 --> 04:18.520
Are you fighting or something?

04:19.480 --> 04:22.650
I forgot to tell it when I'd be coming back.

04:23.190 --> 04:24.490
That's why it's upset with me.

04:25.230 --> 04:27.770
At this rate, it's going to take a while to persuade it.

04:28.310 --> 04:31.200
I'm sorry, but can you let me and Tabunne talk for a bit?

04:37.070 --> 04:38.250
Hey, what should we do?

04:38.650 --> 04:42.970
What we should do...? It'd be great if we could somehow have them make up...

04:45.180 --> 04:45.820
Hey!

04:46.490 --> 04:48.200
Can you persuade Tabunne?

04:48.810 --> 04:49.260
Who're you?

04:49.670 --> 04:50.890
I'm Tsutomu.

04:51.260 --> 04:52.190
I'm Satoshi.

04:52.670 --> 04:53.740
This is my partner Pikachu.

04:55.290 --> 04:56.360
I'm Serena.

04:56.670 --> 04:57.470
I'm Citron.

04:57.900 --> 04:59.080
I'm Eureka.

04:59.390 --> 05:00.490
This little one is Dedenne...

05:01.640 --> 05:02.750
...and this is Squishy.

05:04.460 --> 05:05.450
Nice to meet you.

05:06.860 --> 05:09.980
Can you convince those two to make up?

05:10.310 --> 05:12.540
They're actually good friends, you know.

05:13.740 --> 05:15.250
Tsutomu, do you know anything?

05:15.500 --> 05:16.190
Follow me!

05:19.830 --> 05:20.380
This way.

05:20.990 --> 05:23.070
From here, we can get to where Tabunne is.

05:34.680 --> 05:35.520
Come on, get in!

05:46.200 --> 05:47.860
Hey, Tabunne!

05:48.460 --> 05:50.660
Please, open up!

05:51.130 --> 05:53.770
I'm sorry for being careless and forgetting to call you.

05:56.360 --> 05:57.160
Tabunne!

06:00.220 --> 06:04.170
Don't worry. These people here are worried about you, Tabunne.

06:12.200 --> 06:15.180
Hey, Tabunne. Can't you make up with Joy-san?

06:15.500 --> 06:18.810
At this rate, the people coming to the Pokémon Center will be in trouble.

06:34.990 --> 06:37.260
Hang in there! Hang in there, Makunoshita!

06:37.610 --> 06:39.710
We're almost there, Makunoshita!

06:44.330 --> 06:45.720
Excuse me, Joy-san!

06:45.990 --> 06:47.750
I-I request treatment!

06:48.300 --> 06:49.680
Wh-What should I do...?

06:50.430 --> 06:51.320
Now what?

06:53.310 --> 06:54.100
Let me examine it for a second.

06:54.990 --> 06:56.630
Y-You are...

06:58.400 --> 06:59.600
...Professor Platane...?

07:01.710 --> 07:04.440
This requires urgent attention.

07:05.350 --> 07:06.860
It needs to be treated immediately.

07:07.150 --> 07:08.110
Y-Yes!

07:08.870 --> 07:11.770
Tabunne, open this door! There's an emergency patient!

07:15.350 --> 07:16.160
Make preparations immediately!

07:18.200 --> 07:18.870
Professor Platane!

07:19.500 --> 07:20.120
Satoshi-kun!

07:20.940 --> 07:23.380
Makunoshita's condition is serious. Will you help me?

07:23.870 --> 07:25.130
Uh, sure.

07:26.830 --> 07:27.160
Yes.

07:32.600 --> 07:34.120
Tabunne, I'm counting on you.

07:37.510 --> 07:38.600
Pokémon Quiz!

07:39.810 --> 07:40.550
The answer is...?

08:10.710 --> 08:11.840
What about Makunoshita?

08:12.040 --> 08:13.210
It's still in treatment.

08:13.560 --> 08:14.700
What is its condition?

08:15.110 --> 08:16.810
Let's leave the rest to the two of them.

08:17.820 --> 08:19.220
There's no need to worry.

08:27.340 --> 08:27.930
What's this?

08:28.220 --> 08:29.690
Joy-san found this.

08:30.190 --> 08:31.360
A Mega Stone!

08:39.310 --> 08:40.790
It'll be fine now.

08:43.750 --> 08:44.460
Makunoshita!

08:45.790 --> 08:46.940
Thank goodness.

08:47.910 --> 08:49.310
Okay, you got me.

08:49.670 --> 08:52.620
Joy-san, Tabunne, thank you very much.

08:54.330 --> 08:56.110
You're welcome.

08:57.400 --> 08:58.390
Take care.

09:02.990 --> 09:05.110
All right, let's clean up, Tabunne.

09:08.920 --> 09:11.630
I'm so glad Makunoshita got better.

09:11.850 --> 09:13.590
Joy-san is very skillful.

09:14.270 --> 09:17.080
Not just that, but she and her assistant Tabunne make a good team.

09:17.930 --> 09:19.990
See? I told you they're good friends.

09:19.990 --> 09:22.080
But they fight all the time, right?

09:23.070 --> 09:25.320
There must be a reason.

09:26.060 --> 09:28.920
By the way, Professor Platane, about Squishy...

09:29.160 --> 09:32.810
That's right! I need to actually physically examine it to know more.

09:33.390 --> 09:35.290
Can you show it to me right away?

09:35.290 --> 09:37.470
Eureka is taking care of it.

09:37.990 --> 09:38.490
Yep!

09:39.740 --> 09:40.810
Squishy...

09:41.500 --> 09:43.430
Be still for a second.

09:44.950 --> 09:46.710
Squishy, nice to meet you.

09:48.440 --> 09:49.580
It's fine.

09:49.990 --> 09:53.320
I see. It really is squishy.

09:53.740 --> 09:55.290
That's why it's called Squishy.

09:59.690 --> 10:01.450
What do you think, Professor Platane?

10:01.900 --> 10:02.990
Is it a new species?

10:03.480 --> 10:04.990
I can't say anything for sure yet, but...

10:05.390 --> 10:10.390
Ever since you called me the other day, I've sent inquiries to multiple research institutions,

10:12.310 --> 10:14.630
but there's never been anything like it before.

10:16.270 --> 10:19.470
I need to investigate its cells in detail on a genetic level...

10:20.710 --> 10:22.970
...before I can draw any conclusions.

10:24.390 --> 10:26.480
Just who <i>are</i> you?

10:29.290 --> 10:31.290
But I apologized!

10:35.210 --> 10:35.990
Oh boy...

10:36.380 --> 10:37.630
They're fighting again.

10:37.870 --> 10:40.010
Both of you, please calm down!

10:40.520 --> 10:40.920
Hmph!

10:42.250 --> 10:44.160
Why do you fight so much?

10:44.600 --> 10:48.160
Before we were assigned to this Pokémon Center...

10:56.650 --> 10:57.430
A Tabunne?!

10:59.870 --> 11:01.610
Everyone's got a Pukurin;

11:02.680 --> 11:04.510
why did I get paired up with a Tabunne?!

11:04.890 --> 11:10.560
When you're focused on something specific, you seem to have a tendency to forget everything around you.

11:10.940 --> 11:11.420
What?!

11:12.330 --> 11:17.820
That's why I decided to pair you up with this veteran assistant Tabunne as a special favor.

11:18.330 --> 11:20.280
N-No way...

11:20.870 --> 11:23.190
This Tabunne has a lot of experience.

11:23.630 --> 11:26.810
Its prowess is at chief nurse-level, so to speak,

11:27.050 --> 11:30.040
so I'm sure it'll help you.

11:31.480 --> 11:33.580
What?!

11:33.900 --> 11:36.940
I think things through before I do them,

11:37.610 --> 11:40.510
but Tabunne keeps meddling with my business.

11:42.570 --> 11:46.850
Uh, I guess that means you both have a strong sense of responsibility?

11:47.450 --> 11:50.180
Joy-san, there's something I'd like to ask you.

11:52.010 --> 11:54.650
You found this, right?

11:55.910 --> 11:56.890
That's...

11:59.690 --> 12:03.510
I was thinking about ways to achieve even better treatments with Tabunne...

12:04.120 --> 12:05.590
...when I encountered this book.

12:08.010 --> 12:10.250
That's the book about Mega Evolution that I've written.

12:10.700 --> 12:11.100
Yes.

12:11.710 --> 12:14.750
That's how I came to know that Tabunne can mega evolve.

12:16.220 --> 12:17.750
Tabunne mega evolves?!

12:18.470 --> 12:19.590
Have there been reports of that?

12:20.140 --> 12:20.590
Yeah.

12:20.940 --> 12:28.780
That's when I got the idea to use Mega Evolution to increase Tabunne's healing power and put it to use during treatments.

12:30.950 --> 12:33.270
So that's why you went to find the Mega Stone.

12:34.670 --> 12:35.240
Yes.

12:37.320 --> 12:40.060
In that case, why didn't you tell Tabunne before going out...?

12:40.060 --> 12:41.430
I wanted to surprise it!

12:42.010 --> 12:46.650
I wanted to keep it a secret until I found the Mega Stone and then present it to Tabunne.

12:46.650 --> 12:48.990
Whoa, so you planned a surprise!

12:51.110 --> 12:52.500
I'm sorry, Tabunne.

12:52.910 --> 12:59.020
All right, now that the misunderstanding is cleared up, I happen to have a miniature synchronizer for investigations...

12:59.950 --> 13:02.760
Let's check what kind of Mega Stone you've found.

13:03.350 --> 13:04.220
Please do!

13:08.310 --> 13:10.760
There are lots of monster balls.

13:11.820 --> 13:14.630
Let's take them all!

13:14.630 --> 13:16.440
It's time for our secret weapon to take its turn!

13:16.700 --> 13:18.060
Hm? What, what?

13:18.360 --> 13:19.560
Raise the volume!

13:19.800 --> 13:21.450
...Mega Stone you've found.

13:21.790 --> 13:22.830
"Mega Stone"?

13:22.830 --> 13:23.990
Did he say "Mega Stone"?!

13:48.940 --> 13:51.430
There's no doubt. This is a Tabunnenite.

13:51.980 --> 13:52.910
Really?

13:56.570 --> 13:57.190
Tabunne.

13:58.030 --> 13:59.690
You should hold on to this.

14:01.480 --> 14:03.440
I'm sure it'll be of use at some point.

14:08.940 --> 14:09.720
What?!

14:10.110 --> 14:10.990
Did that come from the garden?

14:13.820 --> 14:14.680
A monster ball?

14:20.810 --> 14:22.040
What are you doing?!

14:22.810 --> 14:24.550
Oh no! The Pokémon...!

14:24.730 --> 14:26.390
There's lots of them!

14:26.700 --> 14:28.300
A mountain full of treasures!

14:28.810 --> 14:30.010
Not you guys again!

14:30.220 --> 14:31.870
Stop it, auntie!

14:32.180 --> 14:34.860
If you tell us "Stop it, sweet young girl!",

14:34.860 --> 14:36.950
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

14:37.470 --> 14:39.440
To prevent the world's destruction!

14:39.880 --> 14:41.790
To protect the world's peace!

14:42.220 --> 14:44.990
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

14:45.770 --> 14:47.670
we're lovely, charmy villains!

14:48.750 --> 14:49.480
Musashi!

14:49.820 --> 14:50.490
Kojiro!

14:50.990 --> 14:53.950
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

14:54.430 --> 14:57.080
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

14:57.080 --> 14:58.680
Just kidding!

15:01.270 --> 15:02.280
What's this "Rocket Gang"?

15:02.760 --> 15:04.880
They're bad people who steal Pokémon from others.

15:05.080 --> 15:06.760
Then those Pokémon are...!

15:06.940 --> 15:09.640
Exactly! We'll take them all!

15:09.930 --> 15:14.190
We have improved Mega Mega Evolution, which already surpassed the capabilities of Mega Evolution, even further!

15:14.190 --> 15:17.130
This truly can be called the ultimate Giga Mega Evolution mecha!

15:17.400 --> 15:19.320
Its name is "Giga Giga Nyarth"!

15:19.870 --> 15:24.390
We originally just planned to take the monster balls from the Pokémon Center,

15:24.710 --> 15:28.460
but considering Pikachu rushed to its doom on its own, we're changing up our plan and taking it too!

15:28.940 --> 15:34.700
On top of that, when we heard you talking about Mega Evolution earlier, we thought we'd take the Mega Stone as well!

15:34.970 --> 15:36.090
That's the story.

15:36.090 --> 15:37.020
Come on, Nyarth!

15:37.020 --> 15:38.380
Got it!

15:42.110 --> 15:43.670
Giga Giga Nyarth, activate!

15:43.670 --> 15:44.420
Start up!

15:44.420 --> 15:45.600
Operate!

15:49.580 --> 15:50.220
Nyarth!

15:50.220 --> 15:51.510
Collect them, collect them!

15:51.510 --> 15:52.670
Understood!

15:55.130 --> 15:55.750
Satoshi-kun!

15:59.180 --> 16:00.550
Wait a second!

16:02.680 --> 16:04.150
Hm? What is it?

16:04.760 --> 16:06.780
This is our Pokémon Center.

16:07.160 --> 16:08.710
We won't let you do as you please!

16:10.620 --> 16:12.760
Oh right. We need that too!

16:12.760 --> 16:13.990
Got it.

16:14.310 --> 16:15.610
Let's go, Tabunne!

16:18.760 --> 16:19.310
I knew it...

16:21.160 --> 16:22.080
Joy-san, take this!

16:26.940 --> 16:28.950
By now, you and Tabunne can do it.

16:29.710 --> 16:33.680
The moment your hearts become one is when Mega Evolution occurs!

16:34.360 --> 16:34.940
Tabunne!

16:37.070 --> 16:39.190
How convenient everything's all in one place.

16:39.190 --> 16:40.750
Go for it, Nyarth!

16:41.020 --> 16:41.890
Got it!

16:43.190 --> 16:44.630
Joy-san! Tabunne!

16:45.610 --> 16:46.380
Watch out!

16:46.380 --> 16:47.020
Run!

16:48.940 --> 16:49.590
Tabunne!

16:51.190 --> 16:52.230
Mega evolve!

17:18.030 --> 17:19.220
So this is Tabunne's...

17:19.220 --> 17:20.310
...Mega Evolution...

17:21.750 --> 17:22.910
Amazing!

17:22.910 --> 17:24.330
What a pretty Forme!

17:24.330 --> 17:25.980
It is incredibly wonderful!

17:26.550 --> 17:27.580
Marvelous!

17:28.060 --> 17:30.320
I knew those two had a strong bond.

17:34.220 --> 17:35.950
Somehow, I have a bad feeling about this...

17:36.550 --> 17:39.900
Musashi, let's not get greedy and run now...

17:40.280 --> 17:42.790
I think so too.

17:42.790 --> 17:45.100
Tabunne, save Satoshi-kun and Pikachu!

17:45.560 --> 17:46.600
Power-Up Punch!

17:55.560 --> 17:57.110
Tabunne, Double Slap!

18:01.990 --> 18:03.450
Th-That's powerful!

18:03.900 --> 18:04.490
Now!

18:04.910 --> 18:05.390
Take Down!

18:08.650 --> 18:09.730
Power-Up Punch!

18:14.390 --> 18:16.510
It's strong... <i>Too</i> strong...

18:16.900 --> 18:17.580
To finish them off,

18:18.310 --> 18:20.430
use your greatest Heal Pulse!

18:29.660 --> 18:32.410
Somehow, this feels <i>really</i> good...

18:32.760 --> 18:34.440
It's healing my soul...

18:37.400 --> 18:38.300
Somehow, I feel like...

18:39.000 --> 18:40.770
...we should just stop fighting, don't you agree?

18:41.230 --> 18:41.880
You're right.

18:42.280 --> 18:45.280
Let's leave the Pokémon we captured behind!

18:45.480 --> 18:46.830
That's right, that's right!

18:46.830 --> 18:48.830
That's a good idea!

18:55.470 --> 18:57.160
All right, Thunderbolt!

19:07.960 --> 19:08.650
We're going home!

19:19.850 --> 19:21.100
Thank you very much.

19:21.420 --> 19:26.460
Thanks to you, Satoshi-kun and his friends, Tabunne and I were able to make up.

19:28.070 --> 19:29.800
Please don't fight any more.

19:31.270 --> 19:31.720
We won't.

19:33.580 --> 19:36.680
From now on, I intend to let it know before going out.

19:39.030 --> 19:41.360
Professor, what will you do next?

19:42.870 --> 19:47.260
I'll return to the laboratory for now to do research on Squishy.

19:48.430 --> 19:49.370
Please do.

19:50.430 --> 19:50.810
I will.

19:51.450 --> 19:53.710
Until then, please take care of Squishy, Eureka.

19:54.190 --> 19:54.600
I will!

19:56.060 --> 19:58.810
All right, we'll be heading to Eisetsu City.

20:00.590 --> 20:01.590
Well then, let's meet again!

20:01.590 --> 20:02.190
Yes!

20:03.750 --> 20:12.030
Having witnessed the bond between Joy-san and Tabunne, Satoshi and his friends set off for Eisetsu City, aiming for the eighth badge.

20:16.020 --> 20:20.970
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

20:16.020 --> 20:20.970
Sunday November 15th at 8am!

20:17.050 --> 20:19.590
Pokénchi airs Sundays at 8am!

20:24.110 --> 20:25.410
Pokémon Twenty Four Hours!

20:26.340 --> 20:30.770
All right, in today's "Pokémon Twenty Four Hours", we're going to give a detailed report on Pokémon Centers all throughout the world.

20:31.590 --> 20:35.620
The Pokémon acting as Joy-san's partner differs from region to region.

20:34.070 --> 20:37.140
Lucky

20:36.130 --> 20:40.070
For the most part, in Kanto, Jouto, Houen and Sinnoh, you have Lucky or Happinas,

20:37.140 --> 20:40.070
Happinas

20:40.070 --> 20:43.080
Tabunne

20:40.530 --> 20:41.730
in Isshu, you have Tabunne,

20:42.190 --> 20:45.040
and in Kalos, you have Pukurin serving in this role.

20:43.080 --> 20:46.080
Pukurin

20:45.760 --> 20:51.120
I've heard that in rare cases, immature Joy-san are paired with experienced Pokémon.

20:52.500 --> 20:57.300
Uh, yeah... Anyway, thanks to their hard work,

20:57.300 --> 21:00.150
we can leave our Pokémon in their care without worrying.

21:01.310 --> 21:08.150
This Pokémon Center is the current hot topic on the streets because you can be treated with Tabunne's Heal Pulse here.

21:09.350 --> 21:10.770
Tabunne, open up!

21:10.770 --> 21:13.870
I'm sorry for eating all the candy!

21:18.210 --> 21:20.100
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.260 --> 21:21.380
Towards our next adventure!

21:21.990 --> 21:23.940
A Shishiko and a Kaenjishi are fighting!

21:23.940 --> 21:27.780
No, that Shishiko is just trying to become independent by leaving its parents.

21:28.130 --> 21:29.220
So let us watch over it.

21:29.440 --> 21:31.090
But Shishiko is hurt!

21:31.090 --> 21:31.510
What?!

21:31.970 --> 21:34.110
I can't just stand there and watch!

21:34.110 --> 21:34.810
Satoshi!

21:35.630 --> 21:38.190
